        "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{R}={a,b,c,e}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{S}={1,3,9},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{R\\cap S}?$",
        "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{R\\cap S}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{R}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{S}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{R\\cap S} & =\\overset{\u2015}{R}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{S} \\\\  & ={a,b,c,e}\\cup {1,3,9} \\\\  & ={a,b,c,e,1,3,9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
